{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And they brought him hastily out of the pit.</b> As is the way of every deliverance of HaShem, which comes about in an instant, as it says: כִּי קְרוֹבָה יְשׁוּעָתִי לָבוֹא (Isaiah 56:1), and as it says: לוּ עַמִּי שׁוֹמֵעַ לִי וגו׳ כִּמְעַט אוֹיְבֵיהֶם אַכְנִיעַ (Psalms 81:14–15). So too was the matter of Egypt, as it says: כִּי גֹרְשׁוּ מִמִּצְרָיִם (Exodus 12:39), as the Sages of blessed memory said, that their dough did not have time to leaven, etc. And so He said He will do in the future, as it says: וּפִתְאוֹם יָבוֹא אֶל הֵיכָלוֹ הָאָדוֹן אֲשֶׁר אַתֶּם מְבַקְשִׁים וגו׳ (Malachi 3:1)." "<b>And he changed his garments.</b> For one may not enter the king's gate in sackcloth (Esther 4:2)."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:34:09.668521772Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}